WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:24.040
The children arrived at the castle and found Mabel's aunt reading a romance novel.

2
00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:29.377
"Excuse me," said Gerald, "I believe you've lost your niece."

3
00:00:29.378 --> 00:00:33.009
"I didn't lose Mabel. She left."

4
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.677
"Did you get her note?" asked Kathleen.

5
00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:40.802
"Yes, and I'm happy she's living with a rich lady."

6
00:00:40.803 --> 00:00:43.974
Jimmy couldn't be quiet a moment longer.

7
00:00:43.975 --> 00:00:46.887
He had to tell Mabel's aunt the truth.

8
00:00:46.888 --> 00:00:50.816
"Mabel's invisible! She's standing right beside me."

9
00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:55.257
"Don't lie to me!" The aunt glared at Jimmy.

10
00:00:55.258 --> 00:00:56.896
"Please remove this boy.

11
00:00:56.897 --> 00:00:59.792
I'm quite happy about Mabel."

12
00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.590
"Well!" said Gerald.

13
00:01:02.591 --> 00:01:07.587
He was puzzled by this aunt who didn't care about her missing niece.

14
00:01:07.588 --> 00:01:10.969
"But what will Mabel's parents say?"

15
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.412
"Mabel's parents are dead," the aunt said calmly.

16
00:01:15.413 --> 00:01:19.000
The children talked to Mabel's aunt for a few more minutes.

17
00:01:19.001 --> 00:01:23.139
She gave them permission to wander over the castle grounds.

18
00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.951
But she still didn't seem concerned about Mabel.

19
00:01:26.952 --> 00:01:31.080
"Good-bye, children," she said and went back to reading.

20
00:01:31.081 --> 00:01:34.402
When the children were outside again, Mabel said,

21
00:01:34.403 --> 00:01:36.337
"I knew she'd believe my note.

22
00:01:36.338 --> 00:01:38.607
She reads lots of romance novels.

23
00:01:38.608 --> 00:01:41.902
Strange things always happen in her books."

24
00:01:41.903 --> 00:01:46.804
Mabel suggested they walk to the Temple of Flora.

25
00:01:46.805 --> 00:01:48.655
When they were seated, she said,

26
00:01:48.656 --> 00:01:52.323
"I'm hungry, and you can't keep stealing food for me.

27
00:01:52.324 --> 00:01:55.436
I'll have to pretend to be a ghost in the castle."

28
00:01:55.437 --> 00:02:01.156
"You must stay with us until you can remove the ring," Kathleen said kindly.

29
00:02:01.157 --> 00:02:05.199
"I think we need to earn some money for food," said Mabel.

30
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.865
"Let's go to the fair.

31
00:02:06.866 --> 00:02:09.704
Gerald can do magic tricks for money."

32
00:02:09.705 --> 00:02:13.341
"But I don't know any tricks!" said Gerald.

33
00:02:13.342 --> 00:02:17.436
"Don't worry," said Mabel. "I'm invisible.

34
00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.731
I can make it look like you're doing tricks."

35
00:02:20.732 --> 00:02:23.557
The fair was about half a mile away.

36
00:02:23.558 --> 00:02:26.777
Soon they could hear music from the carousel.

37
00:02:26.778 --> 00:02:32.448
Kathleen and Jimmy blended into the crowd while Gerald and Mabel stood in front of a tent.

38
00:02:32.449 --> 00:02:36.078
"Ladies and gentlemen," called out Gerald.

39
00:02:36.079 --> 00:02:40.362
"My invisible assistant can make money disappear."

40
00:02:40.363 --> 00:02:44.856
A crowd began to gather, and Kathleen and Jimmy joined in.

41
00:02:44.857 --> 00:02:47.924
Gerald laid nine pennies on the ground.

42
00:02:47.925 --> 00:02:53.158
Mabel picked them up and put them in her pocket to make them disappear.

43
00:02:53.159 --> 00:02:55.476
The audience clapped.

44
00:02:55.477 --> 00:03:00.495
"If you want to see more magic, I'll need to see more money," said Gerald.

45
00:03:00.496 --> 00:03:03.772
The audience dropped more coins onto the ground.

46
00:03:03.773 --> 00:03:06.632
Then Mabel made more things vanish.

47
00:03:06.633 --> 00:03:13.080
Other things appeared to move around by themselves.

48
00:03:13.081 --> 00:03:17.917
"For my final trick, I will vanish!" said Gerald.

49
00:03:17.918 --> 00:03:22.691
He stepped back, and Mabel wrapped her shawl around him.

50
00:03:22.692 --> 00:03:24.734
But nothing happened.

51
00:03:24.735 --> 00:03:27.575
"He can't do it!" someone yelled.

52
00:03:27.576 --> 00:03:30.571
The crowd pushed forward in anger.

53
00:03:30.572 --> 00:03:35.039
"I wish I could put you in my pocket," Mabel whispered to Gerald.

54
00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.927
"Then you'd be invisible."

55
00:03:36.928 --> 00:03:39.566
She squeezed her hands together.

56
00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.555
"Hey! The ring is loose!"

57
00:03:42.556 --> 00:03:45.957
"Come on!" shouted a man in the crowd.

58
00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.562
"We paid for a show."

59
00:03:48.563 --> 00:03:51.967
Gerald whispered to Mabel, "Go into the tent.

60
00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:54.733
Slip the ring under the canvas to me.

61
00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:59.922
When I see you in the crowd, I'll make myself disappear and catch up with you."

62
00:03:59.923 --> 00:04:04.337
Mabel did just that.

63
00:04:04.338 --> 00:04:09.148
"I'm back," she said to a surprised Kathleen and Jimmy.

64
00:04:09.149 --> 00:04:10.777
"Gerald's wearing the ring.

65
00:04:10.778 --> 00:04:13.102
Let's get out of here."

66
00:04:13.103 --> 00:04:22.254
As the children walked away, they heard Gerald announce, "Now I will vanish."

67
00:04:22.255 --> 00:04:28.306
Then the crowd roared, and the children knew he had really disappeared this time.

68
00:04:28.307 --> 00:04:35.343
After a few minutes, they heard footsteps on the road but saw no one.

69
00:04:35.344 --> 00:04:38.944
"Hello, I'm over here," said Gerald.

70
00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:43.324
"Good," said Mabel. "I want my ring back."

71
00:04:43.325 --> 00:04:46.596
"Well, you can't have it," Gerald answered.

72
00:04:46.597 --> 00:04:52.921
"Because I can't get it off!"
